{%- comment -%}
  "Visualize in Your Space" — trigger for the TilesView modal.

  Rendered twice: once under the desktop media gallery, once above the
  order-a-sample button on mobile. The two live in different columns that swap
  order on mobile, so a single element can't sit in both places. Both share the
  [data-tilesview-trigger] hook, which <tilesview-popup> listens for on
  `document`, so one modal instance serves either button.

  Renders nothing unless the product carries a TilesView product id.

  @param product - the current product
  @param device  - 'desktop' (default) or 'mobile'; picks the visibility class
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if product.metafields.tileview.product_id != blank -%}
  {%- if device == 'mobile' -%}
    {%- assign visibility_class = 'media-visualize-btn--mobile up-mobile-only' -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign visibility_class = 'up-desktop-only' -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  <button type="button" class="media-visualize-btn {{ visibility_class }}" data-tilesview-trigger>
    {%- render 'icon-visualize' -%}
    Visualize in Your Space
  </button>
{%- endif -%}
